{"user": "okay so what's the biggest lesson here for endgames? dont let them get the edge files?", "user_ts": "2026-08-11T22:32:04.227411+00:00", "assistant": "Yes \u2014 but more precise:\n\n**Endgame lesson:** don\u2019t just ask \u201chow many do I flip now?\u201d Ask:\n\n1. **Does my move give White a corner or stable edge/file?**  \n   Once White got the **a-file**, many of those discs became hard/impossible to win back.\n\n2. **Does my move leave White with a powerful reply?**  \n   A \u201cgood-looking\u201d move can lose if it gives White the one move that sweeps a whole line.\n\n3. **Count final discs, not immediate flips.**  \n   In this game Black ended **24\u201340**, so White\u2019s edge/file control mattered far more than a short-term flip.\n\nSo: **don\u2019t blindly avoid all edges**\u2014edges can be good. But in endgames, avoid giving your opponent an edge/file that becomes stable, especially connected to a corner.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-11T22:32:04.227411+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-11T22:32:09.227411+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Conversational Acknowledgment", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Conversational Acknowledgment", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Conversational Acknowledgment": 3, "Solution Request": 1, "Think Aloud": 1, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 2, "Common Ground Question": 1}, "confidence": {"Conversational Acknowledgment": 1.0, "Solution Request": 0.3333333333333333, "Think Aloud": 0.3333333333333333, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 0.6666666666666666, "Common Ground Question": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Conversational Acknowledgment", "Solution Request"], "llama": ["Think Aloud", "Conversational Acknowledgment", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Conversational Acknowledgment", "Knowledge Deficit Question", "Common Ground Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine